											<h4>Tax treaty Chile &#8211; Netherlands explained</h4>
											<div class="datos-evento">
												<span><img class="lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201%201'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://www.investchile.gob.cl/wp-content/themes/invest/images/ic-ev1.png" /> 24-03-2021 10:00 am</span>
												<span><img class="lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201%201'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://www.investchile.gob.cl/wp-content/themes/invest/images/ic-ev2.png" /> Virtual event</span>
												<span><img class="lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201%201'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://www.investchile.gob.cl/wp-content/themes/invest/images/ic-ev3.png" /> <a href="https://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ZMSsLQAXSuqdyd55vY_MjQ" target="_blank">https://us02web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ZMSsLQAXSuqdyd55vY_MjQ</a></span>
											</div>
											<p>Chile and The Netherlands signed a tax treaty, preventing double taxation. After ratification by both parliaments, this treaty will be operational (expected end 2021). In this webinar we will try to explain the why, the what and the how. Speakers from both negotiation teams, from export and investment promotion bureaus and concrete examples of &#8220;before&#8221; [&hellip;]</p>

