										</div>
										<div class="contenido-evento">
											<h4>Gualapack Chile to inaugurate production plant</h4>
											<div class="datos-evento">
												<span><img class="lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201%201'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://www.investchile.gob.cl/wp-content/themes/invest/images/ic-ev1.png" /> 18-04-2018 11:30 am</span>
												<span><img class="lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201%201'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://www.investchile.gob.cl/wp-content/themes/invest/images/ic-ev2.png" /> Parque Los Maitenes 1350, ENEA.</span>
												<span><img class="lazy" src="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%20viewBox='0%200%201%201'%3E%3C/svg%3E" data-src="https://www.investchile.gob.cl/wp-content/themes/invest/images/ic-ev3.png" /> <a href="https://gualapackgroup.com/" target="_blank">https://gualapackgroup.com/</a></span>
											</div>
											<p>Italy’s GualapackGroup, a world leader in flexible packaging technology, will inaugurate its new production plant in Santiago’s Pudahuel district on April 18 at 11:30 in Parque Los Maitenes 1350, ENEA. The event will be headed by the CEO of Gualapack Chile, Salo Himmelstern, and will be attended by the acting director of InvestChile, Ian Frederick. [&hellip;]</p>

